# The one-argument call runs a Structure over itself and takes no other Structure as its data (the book,
# call-receivers): the places declared apart from Code, in CodeData, are not fields of Code itself, so the data lacks
# the variable the code uses -- answer 3. The data is passed explicitly, before the code: `call: CodeData Code`.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds the call main().
# The old text kept the places in a child block `data:` of Code, which the one-argument call does not select; the pair
# is written apart.
sub: main () (
    CodeData:
        int: x 1
    Code:
        x := x + 1
)
    call: Code
main()
